{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Come now, and I will send you, etc.</b> The reason it was necessary to say <b>and I will send you</b> appears unnecessary, for presumably when He says to him ״come now״ it is certain that He is the one sending him. Also, He placed the going before mention of the mission, to say that this going alone is not the mission, but after the going will come the continuation of the mission — as indeed it was, for after he went, He sent him time after time to bring out, etc." "Further, He hinted to him that he would not bring out the children of Israel through this going alone, but rather there would be mission after mission, and the intention in this is that He would yet make him hear that Pharaoh would not consent to send them out immediately and at once." "It further intends, on the basis of what they said (Makkot 10b): 'In the way a person wants to go, he is led' — therefore He said to him <b>come now</b>, meaning: if you desire this mitzvah to go, then I will fulfill your wish and I will send you. And from this you learn that if he had refused to go, He would not have sent him." "<b>Or perhaps</b> it is for this reason that Moshe responded with arguments, since he did not see the word of a sovereign ruler — but rather, if he wished, he would reveal his mind that he has objections preventing him, and HaShem would answer him on each and every objection, so that he would go of his own knowledge and will, as I will explain in what follows." "It further intends, after the manner of what I explained in parashat Vayeshev regarding the mission of Yaakov to Yosef (Genesis 37:13) — meaning: ״come now״ — and if you feel a mishap coming, ״and I will send you״ — and those sent on a mitzvah are not harmed. And this is what stood for him on the way at the inn (Exodus 4:24), that the angel did not kill him."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:57.554913087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}